{
  "manufacturer": "Contemporary Controls",
  "manufacturer_slug": "contemporary-controls",
  "model": "Caterpillar ATC 300+ transfer switch controller via BASgatewayLX",
  "short_model": "BASgatewayLX Cat ATC 300+",
  "model_slug": "basgatewaylx-caterpillar-atc-300-plus",
  "aliases": [
    "ATC 300+",
    "ATC300+",
    "Cat ATS controller",
    "Eaton ATC-300+"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Automatic transfer switch controller",
  "applies_to": "Caterpillar transfer switches with the ATC 300+ controller on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
  "summary": "Gateway profile for the Cat ATC 300+: 111 objects (79 AI, 18 BI, 14 BO), 91 polled by default. Inputs give source available/connected, test and sync states, relay states, lockout and inhibit flags, timers, pickup/dropout settings, source voltages and frequencies, run and connect times, transfer count and primary status. Test, go-to-emergency, retransfer and counter resets are unpolled Binary Outputs.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Cat_ATC300_plus_a_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the ATC 300+ Modbus register list (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/CAT_ATC300plus.pdf).",
    "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
    "Only 91 of the 111 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
    "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
    "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Manual Retransfer); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Cat_ATC300_plus_a",
    "doc_number": "Cat_ATC300_plus_a_LX.csv",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/Cat_ATC300_Plus2.zip"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Read Source 1/2 available and connected, ATS in test and the generator start relay. Enable the test and transfer command outputs only if the BMS is meant to run ATS tests.",
